From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: picture and video details; Quick access remove and reorder

The details pane shows a picture's Dimensions, Width, Height and Bit depth
(WIC) and a video's Length, Frame width and Frame height (Media Foundation),
from the new fileprops.c. Quick access: a frequent folder's context menu (in
the navigation pane and on the Quick access page) starts with "Remove from
Quick access", which drops its count and lists it under the QuickAccess
key's Excluded value so visits do not bring it back. Pinned folders reorder
by dragging them in the navigation pane (an insert mark shows where; Escape
cancels); the Pinned value keeps the new order. Traces for the gate:
"quick access row", "quick access removed", "quick access pin order",
"pane line".

Gate: test/explorer3-gate.sh.
